What Is an Anti-Competitive Agreement?
An anti-competitive agreement is an agreement having appreciable adverse effect on competition. Anti-
competitive agreements include, but are not limited to:-
 l agreement to limit production and/or supply;
 l agreement to allocate markets;
 l agreement to fix price;
 l bid rigging or collusive bidding;
 l conditional purchase/ sale (tie-in arrangement);
 l exclusive supply / distribution arrangement;
 l resale price maintenance; and
 l refusal to deal.
